State Management Rules

- Use Zustand for cross-cutting app/data state and configuration shared across branches of the tree.
- Use Zustand only for ephemeral UI state (e.g., modal visibility, local UI toggles). Do not store server-derived entities in Zustand.
- Prefer query cache (Apollo) and derived selectors over duplicating remote data in local stores.
- Avoid prop drilling only when branching/cross-cutting concerns arise. Linear drilling is acceptable.
- Keep store shape minimal and focused; avoid global singletons for unrelated concerns.
